## Image metadata guidelines (ALT, title, caption)

When adding images to the documentation, every image must include:

- ALT text  
- title attribute  
- figure caption  

Each of these is used by different systems (screen readers, search engines, LLMs, humans) and must be written with a different purpose in mind.
Check [this document](README-image-metadata) for more details if not certain - metadata are important!

---

### 1. ALT text

Who uses it:

- screen readers (accessibility)  
- large language models  
- search engines  
- users with images disabled  

Purpose:

- describe exactly what the image shows

How to write:

- one or two complete sentences  
- factual and neutral  
- describe only what is visually present  
- include relevant Nussknacker terminology where helpful (for example: “scenario node”, “incoming records”, “counts”, “live data view”)  
- do not guess how the UI behaves or what the user should do  
- do not keep it short: ALT text is intentionally descriptive  

Template guidance:

> Describe the visible elements in the image in one or two factual sentences.  
> Include important domain terms.  
> Do not explain meaning or purpose.

---

### 2. Title attribute

Who uses it:

- human users (browser tooltip on hover)

Purpose:

- provide a short label for the image

How to write:

- a few words (3–8)  
- not a full sentence  
- not a description, just a label  

Template guidance:

> A short label shown as a tooltip on hover, for example “Scenario with counts”, “Live data view”, “Test input form”.

---

### 3. Figure caption

Who uses it:

- human readers  
- (secondarily) LLMs

Purpose:

- explain why the image is included on this page

How to write:

- one short sentence  
- explain the role of the image in the surrounding text  
- do not repeat the ALT description  

Template guidance:

> One short sentence explaining why this image is included in the context of this section.

---

### 4. Summary

- ALT: what the image shows (one or two sentences, descriptive).  
- title: a short label (a few words, tooltip).  
- caption: why the image is here (one short sentence).

---

### 5. Example structure (for MDX files)

This example is shown as code so it is not rendered. Use it as a pattern when editing MDX docs:

```mdx
<figure>
  <img
    src={imageImport}
    alt="Descriptive ALT text here (what the image shows)."
    title="Short label here."
  />
  <figcaption>
    One short sentence explaining why the image is included.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

